<%#
  One view, both outcomes. A redirect with a flash message would be the usual
  shape, but flash is stored in the session — and issuing a session cookie is
  the thing these public pages go out of their way not to do.

  subscriber is nil when the honeypot was filled: a bot gets the same page a
  person does, and learns nothing.
%>
<% failed = subscriber&.errors&.any? %>

<% content_for :title, failed ? "That address didn't look right — Remindly" : "Check your inbox — Remindly" %>

<% if failed %>
  <h1>That address didn't look right</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    <%= subscriber.errors.full_messages.to_sentence %>. Have another go — or
    just email <a href="mailto:hello@remindly.care">hello@remindly.care</a> and
    I'll add you by hand.
  </p>

  <%= render "shared/subscribe_form", source: "retry" %>
<% else %>
  <h1>Check your inbox</h1>

  <%#
    This page must be true in four situations: a new signup, someone who
    signed up earlier and has not confirmed, someone already on the list, and
    a bot that filled the honeypot. Only the first two are sent an email, and
    the second not if one went out within the hour. So it says what happens
    if the address is new to the list, and cannot tell anyone whether it was.

    The routine sheet is linked directly: it is what they came for, and it
    is public anyway, so nobody has to wait for a confirmation to get it.
  %>
  <p class="lead">
    If this address is not on the list yet, we have emailed it a link to
    confirm. Nothing else is sent until you click it.
  </p>

  <p>
    In the meantime, here is the routine sheet —
    <a href="<%= routine_sheet_path %>">open it and print it</a>. One page for
    the fridge door. No email? You may already be on the list, or it may be
    in the spam folder; write to
    <a href="mailto:hello@remindly.care">hello@remindly.care</a> if in doubt.
  </p>

  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= login_path %>">Try Remindly — it's free</a>
    <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="<%= blog_path %>">Read something first</a>
  </div>
<% end %>
